2026-10-27T11:52:26.9415283Z     [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9415839Z [0m[36m173[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mzstd 0.13.3 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9416808Z     [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9417424Z     [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9417738Z     [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0391
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9418240Z     [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0391
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9418893Z     [0m[36m├[0m The `with_context` constructors of the stream encoders and decoders used the
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9419487Z       borrowed context as it was. When a stream was abandoned on a context, for
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9420058Z       example an encoder dropped before `finish()` after an error, whatever it
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9420584Z       left there was carried into the next stream: the input buffered by the
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9421105Z       previous encoder (up to 128 KiB, or all of it with `zstdmt`) became the
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9421559Z       start of the next frame, and a decoder returned undelivered output of the
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9421939Z       previous stream.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9422146Z       
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9422476Z       An application reusing one context for data that must stay separate, such
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9423146Z       as different users' requests, could disclose one user's plaintext to
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9423680Z       another. Whoever supplies the data can cause the abandonment with invalid
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9424087Z       input.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9424301Z       
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9424591Z       The flaw was corrected by resetting the context's session in
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9425119Z       `with_context`.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9425742Z     [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/commit/74ace2dcdca62a2ce0f034895d6079458311e003
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9426476Z     [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=0.14.3 (try `cargo update -p zstd`)
