2026-10-27T11:52:26.9445861Z [0m[1m[38;5;9merror[vulnerability][0m[1m: Uninitialized memory exposed when streaming decompression of a legacy frame fails[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9446562Z     [0m[36m┌─[0m /github/workspace/Cargo.lock:174:1
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9446933Z     [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9447487Z [0m[36m174[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mzstd-safe 7.2.4 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9448605Z     [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9449185Z     [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9449483Z     [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0403
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9449957Z     [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0403
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9450560Z     [0m[36m├[0m When decompression fails inside a legacy (zstd v0.4 to v0.7) frame, the
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9451143Z       bundled zstd library reports the output buffer as fully written although
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9451717Z       nothing was written. `DCtx::decompress_stream` committed that position even
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9452245Z       on error, and for a `Vec<u8>` destination this extended the vector's length
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9452742Z       over uninitialized memory.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9452954Z       
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9453241Z       Legacy support is enabled by default. A 5- or 6-byte corrupt legacy frame is
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9453722Z       enough: through `zstd::stream::write::Decoder`, up to 32 KiB of stale heap
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9454181Z       memory is then passed to the wrapped writer on the next `write()` or
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9454472Z       `flush()`, or when an `auto_flush()`/`on_flush()` decoder is dropped. Whether
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9454764Z       this reaches an attacker depends on where the application sends the
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9455066Z       decompressed output. `zstd::stream::read::Decoder`, `zstd::decode_all` and
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9455300Z       the bulk API are not affected.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9455453Z       
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9455618Z       Before zstd-safe 4.0.0, output buffers could only be initialized slices.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9455909Z       The zstd crate's own writer had the same flaw from 0.4.22 to 0.7.x, which is
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9456149Z       covered by a separate advisory.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9456306Z       
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9456571Z       The flaw was corrected by only committing the buffer positions of a
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9456798Z       successful call.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9457143Z     [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/commit/006e1d1ad1eeaf6b5d4c28329e70217adabcec43
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9457541Z     [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=8.2.0 (try `cargo update -p zstd-safe`)
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9457788Z     [0m[36m├[0m zstd-safe v7.2.4
