2026-10-27T11:52:26.9459739Z [0m[1m[38;5;9merror[vulnerability][0m[1m: WebAssembly allocator shim corrupts memory on allocation failure[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9460104Z     [0m[36m┌─[0m /github/workspace/Cargo.lock:175:1
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9460280Z     [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9460611Z [0m[36m175[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mzstd-sys 2.0.16+zstd.1.5.7 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9461161Z     [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9461514Z     [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9461698Z     [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0410
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9461955Z     [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0410
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9462309Z     [0m[36m├[0m On wasm32, zstd-sys provides `malloc` and `free` to the C library through a
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9463131Z       shim over Rust's allocator. The shim did not check for allocation failure:
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9463615Z       it wrote its size header to address 0 and returned address 4, which the C
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9463959Z       library used as a valid buffer. `free(NULL)` also read below address 0.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9464183Z       
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9464351Z       Whenever the instance cannot grow its memory by what a frame asks for, a
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9464666Z       small crafted frame (a 9-byte header declaring a 128 MiB window is enough)
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9464966Z       made decompression write decoded data over the bottom of the module's
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9465260Z       linear memory, instead of failing. The corruption stays within the wasm
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9465500Z       sandbox.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9465608Z       
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9465783Z       The flaw was corrected by returning NULL on allocation failure or size
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9466052Z       overflow, and by making `free(NULL)` a no-op.
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9466464Z     [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/commit/165d1625553c236b9700ca794b8a7c51f5d98314
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9466898Z     [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=2.1.2 (try `cargo update -p zstd-sys`)
2026-10-27T11:52:26.9467190Z     [0m[36m├[0m zstd-sys v2.0.16+zstd.1.5.7
